# Trivy findings intentionally ignored for the proxmox-infra repo.
#
# One ID per line — CVE IDs for the image scan in build:<image> (before the
# push), Trivy/AVD misconfig IDs for the Terraform scan (scan:trivy-iac).
# Document WHY inline so an ignore is auditable. Parallels
# .config/.gitleaksignore — repo-local, passed to both via --ignorefile. The
# scans block on CRITICAL findings, so every entry carries an exp: date that
# forces a re-triage.

# semaphore: brotli-libs 1.1.0-r2 in upstream semaphoreui/semaphore's Alpine
# 3.21 base. 3.21 is end of life, so no fixed package will reach its repository.
# Clears when upstream moves to a newer Alpine (Renovate bumps the image).
CVE-2026-111497 exp:2027-01-31

# semaphore: the certifi vendored inside the Ansible venv's own pip (pip
# 26.2.1), used only when pip installs something, which the runner never does.
# The venv's runtime certifi is already 2026.10.18. pip 26.3 (2026-11-02)
# vendors a fixed certifi; pin it once it passes the two-week age rule.
GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2 exp:2026-11-30

# ci-base gitleaks 8.30.1 (the newest release) is built with Go 1.24.11.
# CVE-2025-68121 is in crypto/tls session resumption; CI runs gitleaks only
# over local git history, which opens no TLS connection. Clears when a
# gitleaks release ships a fixed Go (Renovate bumps GITLEAKS_VERSION).
CVE-2025-68121 exp:2027-01-31
